Standard-14 font metrics and encoding tables

PlumePDF's built-in Standard-14 font support (`src/PlumePdf/Fonts/Standard14/`) is
source-generated at development time from Adobe's Core14 AFM (Adobe Font Metrics) files —
the width, bounding-box, and kerning data for the 14 base fonts every PDF viewer must support
without embedding (Helvetica, Times, Courier, Symbol, ZapfDingbats, and their bold/italic/
bold-italic variants). PDFsharp and PdfPig bundle the same files as precedent.

  Source: Adobe Systems Incorporated Core 14 AFM files, distributed under Adobe's own
  AFM (Adobe Font Metrics) license, which permits redistribution and use.

  https://github.com/adobe-type-tools/afdko (font metrics reference) and Adobe's own
  Core 14 font metrics distribution.

No AFM file text or ISO 32000 spec prose is committed to this repository — only the resulting
numeric tables (widths, bounding boxes) are compiled into
`src/PlumePdf/Fonts/Standard14/Standard14Metrics.g.cs`. See `docs/spec-sources.md` for the full
provenance note, including the on-the-record rationale for why transcribing ISO 32000-1 Annex D's
encoding tables (data, not prose) does not implicate the clean-room policy (AGENTS.md).

Adobe is not affiliated with and does not endorse PlumePDF.

