PdfPig — word assembly and reading-order heuristics

PlumePDF's Phase 3 extraction word/line assembly (`src/PlumePdf/Documents/WordAssembler.cs`,
`src/PlumePdf/Documents/ReadingOrderer.cs`) adapts the published shape of two algorithms from
PdfPig's document-layout-analysis module: a nearest-neighbour gap/overlap clustering approach
for grouping letters into words (PdfPig's `NearestNeighbourWordExtractor`), and a
content-order-with-geometric-line-grouping baseline for ordering words into reading order
(PdfPig's `ContentOrderTextExtractor`). Per the clean-room policy (AGENTS.md), this is a
reimplementation from the algorithms' published shape and behavior against PlumePDF's own
`Letter`/`GraphicsStateStack` types — PdfPig's source was not copied; see the provenance
comment at the top of each file for exactly which algorithm's shape it follows.

  Source: PdfPig (UglyToad/PdfPig), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/UglyToad/PdfPig

PdfPig's maintainers are not affiliated with and do not endorse PlumePDF.

