Unicode Character Database — complex-script shaping property tables

PlumePDF's complex-script shaping support (`src/PlumePdf/Fonts/Shaping/UnicodeShapingData.g.cs`)
is source-generated at development time from the Unicode Character Database (UCD): the Script,
Joining_Type, Joining_Group, Indic_Syllabic_Category, Indic_Positional_Category, Bidi_Class,
Bidi_Mirroring, Canonical_Combining_Class, and Grapheme_Cluster_Break property data files, pinned
to one Unicode version (`scripts/generate-unicode-data.csx`'s `UNICODE_VERSION`).

  Source: the Unicode Character Database, Copyright (c) Unicode, Inc. Distributed under the
  Unicode License (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt), which permits use, copying,
  modification, and redistribution with this attribution notice.

  https://www.unicode.org/Public/ — UCD data files
  https://www.unicode.org/reports/ — Unicode Standard Annexes (UAX #9, #14, #24, #29) and
  Unicode Technical Reports (UTR #53), consulted for the algorithms the generated data feeds.

No UCD file text is committed to this repository — the source files are fetched by the
generator script at run time (gitignored, never vendored) and only the resulting
range-compressed numeric/enum tables are compiled into
`src/PlumePdf/Fonts/Shaping/UnicodeShapingData.g.cs`. See `docs/spec-sources.md` for the full
provenance note, including the OpenType specification and Microsoft per-script shaping
documentation citations the shaping engine itself relies on.

The same UCD distribution provides `BidiTest.txt`/`BidiCharacterTest.txt` — the UAX #9
bidirectional-algorithm conformance suites `tests/PlumePdf.CorpusTests/BidiConformanceTests.cs`
runs `BidiAlgorithm` against. Same license, same
"fetched at run time, gitignored, never vendored" treatment — `scripts/fetch-corpora.sh` fetches
both files directly from `https://www.unicode.org/Public/16.0.0/ucd/`, checksum-verified.

The Unicode License V3 is reproduced in full under "Full license texts" below.

Unicode, Inc. is not affiliated with and does not endorse PlumePDF.

