HarfBuzz — shaping-oracle test corpus (curated input text)

PlumePDF's hermetic shaping-oracle test lane (`tests/PlumePdf.CorpusTests/ShapingOracleTests.cs`) curates several real-word Arabic and Devanagari
test strings in the spirit of — and, for a few entries, with the exact codepoint sequences of —
HarfBuzz's own MIT-licensed `test/shape/data/in-house/tests/` corpus (e.g.
`arabic-fallback-shaping.tests`, `indic-syllable.tests`). No HarfBuzz file text or per-test font
is vendored: HarfBuzz's own fixture files pin specific per-test fonts whose glyph IDs/names are
meaningless against PlumePDF's own pinned Noto fixture fonts, so only the input
*codepoints* are drawn from that public corpus — the expected glyph ID/advance/offset data
checked into the test file is PlumePDF's own, captured once against its own fonts via the
`hb-shape` CLI (the same tool `HbShapeInteropTests` runs live as the ARMED external oracle half).

  Source: HarfBuzz (harfbuzz/harfbuzz), licensed under the MIT License.
  https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/tree/main/test/shape/data/in-house/tests

