pdf.js — CCITT, JBIG2, and JPEG codec port shape

PlumePDF's Phase 7 raster codecs (`src/PlumePdf/Filters/CcittFaxEngine.cs`,
`src/PlumePdf/Filters/Jbig2/`, `src/PlumePdf/Filters/Jpeg/`) are clean-room ports of the
published algorithm shape of Mozilla pdf.js's `ccitt.js`, `jbig2.js`, and `jpg.js`, pinned to
release tag `v5.6.205` — the last tag carrying these as plain, readable JavaScript source
before pdf.js's own WASM rewrite moved them to a compiled, unreadable-in-repo form. Per the clean-room policy (AGENTS.md), this is a reimplementation from the algorithms' published shape and
behavior against PlumePDF's own types (`CcittFaxEngine`, `Jbig2Decoder`, `JpegDecoder`, none
of which share a type/method shape with pdf.js's JavaScript) — pdf.js's source was read and
its algorithm structure followed, not copied; see the provenance comment at the top of each
port's implementation file for exactly which upstream file and function it follows.

  Source: pdf.js (mozilla/pdf.js), tag v5.6.205, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/tree/v5.6.205/src/core

Mozilla and the pdf.js contributors are not affiliated with and do not endorse PlumePDF.

