Liberation Fonts — bundled substitute-font faces

PlumePDF's Phase 8 rasterizer falls back to a bundled substitute font when a page's text uses a
non-embedded font (`src/PlumePdf/Fonts/Substitute/`, `tools/FontAssetGen`): twelve faces across the Liberation Sans, Liberation Serif, and Liberation
Mono families (regular/bold/italic/bold-italic each), metric-compatible with Arial/Times New
Roman/Courier New respectively, compiled directly into this package as FieldRVA blobs (`.g.cs`
files, one per face) rather than a separate downloaded/reflection-loaded asset — the same
NativeAOT-safety rationale as `Standard14Metrics.g.cs`.

